      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:7:36:23",
      "text": [
        " اسْتِمَاعُ الْغِنَاءِ وَ اللَّهْوِ يُنْبِتُ النِّفَاقَ فِي الْقَلْبِ كَمَا يُنْبِتُ الْمَاءُ الزَّرْعَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, form Ibn Mahboub, from Anbasa, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Listening to the singing (music) and the vanities grow the hypocrisy in the heart just as the water grows the plantation’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "23. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn Mahbub from ‘ Anbasah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Listening to al-Ghina’ (music (and singing)) and useless things grows hypocrisy just as water grows green plants.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
